{"step_index":536,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:27:41Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-11T20:27:41+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T20:27:41+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/pipeline/lean_export.py`\nTotal Lines: 244\nTotal Bytes: 11198\nShowing lines 1 to 70\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: \"\"\"\n2: pipeline/lean_export.py — well-formed Lean 4 export for the *supported* subset of\n3: CEGIS survivors.\n4: \n5: graffiti3 will happily render any conjecture to a Lean stub, but a stub over\n6: undefined symbols (``domination_number G``) can never be kernel-verified. This\n7: module restricts export to conjectures whose invariants are backed by the\n8: ``LeanProject.GraphInvariants`` preamble (mathlib defs + a small domination\n9: layer), maps each invariant to its real Lean name, and emits a self-contained,\n10: compilable ``theorem … := sorry`` (imports + binders + ``open SimpleGraph``) that\n11: a prover can actually close.\n12: \n13: Out of scope (silently skipped, not mis-formalized): invariants with no faithful\n14: mathlib definition yet (zero forcing, residue, Roman domination, …) and\n15: conjectures conditioned on a graph class with no formalization (chordal, planar).\n16: \"\"\"\n17: from __future__ import annotations\n18: \n19: import re\n20: from typing import Dict, List, Optional\n21: \n22: from pipeline import linear_form\n23: from pipeline.lean_disproof import definedness_hyps\n24: \n25: # pipeline invariant column  →  Lean expression over `(G : SimpleGraph V)`.\n26: # Only invariants with a faithful definition in LeanProject.GraphInvariants (or\n27: # mathlib, re-exported there) appear here.\n28: SUPPORTED: Dict[str, str] = {\n29:     \"order\":                         \"G.order\",\n30:     \"size\":                          \"G.size\",\n31:     \"minimum_degree\":                \"G.minDegree\",\n32:     \"maximum_degree\":                \"G.maxDegree\",\n33:     \"cli\n<truncated 365 bytes>\n   \"zero_forcing_number\":           \"G.zeroForcingNumber\",\n40:     \"total_zero_forcing_number\":     \"G.totalZeroForcingNumber\",\n41:     \"connected_zero_forcing_number\": \"G.connectedZeroForcingNumber\",\n42:     \"vertex_cover_number\":            \"(G.vertexCoverNum).toNat\",\n43:     \"total_domination_number\":       \"G.totalDominationNumber\",\n44:     \"edge_cover_number\":             \"G.edgeCoverNumber\",\n45:     \"sub_total_domination_number\":   \"G.subTotalDominationNumber\",\n46:     \"roman_domination_number\":       \"G.romanDominationNumber\",\n47:     \"double_roman_domination_number\": \"G.doubleRomanDominationNumber\",\n48:     \"radius\":                        \"(G.radius).toNat\",\n49: }\n50: \n51: # Injected binders: a finite vertex type with decidable adjacency, enough for\n52: # every invariant above to elaborate.\n53: _HEADER_BINDERS = (\"{V : Type*} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\n\"\n54:                    \"    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\")\n55: \n56: _PREAMBLE = \"import Mathlib\\nimport LeanProject.GraphInvariants\\n\\nopen SimpleGraph\\n\"\n57: \n58: _SIG_RE = re.compile(r\"theorem\\s+(\\w+)\\s*\\(G\\s*:\\s*SimpleGraph\\s+V\\)\")\n59: \n60: # graph-class column → preamble predicate. The remaining unformalized classes\n61: # are chordal and planar: neither has a mathlib definition or a cheap decidable\n62: # characterization, so conjectures conditioned on them stay unexportable.\n63: CLASS_PREDICATES = {\n64:     \"regular\": \"IsRegularClass\", \"cubic\": \"IsCubicClass\",\n65:     \"subcubic\": \"IsSubcubicClass\", \"triangle_free\": \"IsTriangleFreeClass\",\n66:     \"K_4_free\": \"IsK4FreeClass\", \"bipartite\": \"IsBipartiteClass\",\n67:     \"eulerian\": \"IsEulerianClass\",\n68:     # mathlib has these directly (`Connected`, `IsTree`)\n69:     \"connected\": \"IsConnectedClass\", \"tree\": \"IsTreeClass\",\n70:     # forbidden induced subgraph on four vertices: K₁,₃ and P₄ respectively\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
